<title>USA: N.J. Gov. vetoes bill on investing in mutual funds.</title>
<headline>N.J. Gov. vetoes bill on investing in mutual funds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Jersey Gov. Christine Whitman conditionally vetoed a bill that would allow school boards and local governments to invest in mutual funds.</p>
<p>The Governor recommended lawmakers add provisions to the proposed legislation that would &quot;ensure prudent investing&quot; if the measure became law, according to a statement issued by the governor's office.</p>
<p>The measure now heads back to the Legislature for possible amendments.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
